    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `GOLD` membership tier rule: an owner becomes `GOLD` when their household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3 or more members after that owner is created; otherwise the existing `SILVER`/`BRONZE` rules apply.\n\nFollowing the codebase's existing pattern (`namesakeCount`, `bulkSignupWarning` are snapshotted on the owner at create time and read back by the mapper), I:\n\n1. **Schema** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 added a `household_size` column to the `owners` table. The test runs on the `hsqldb` profile with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column has to exist in the SQL schema.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `householdSize` field (`@Column(name = \"household_size\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, after the household id is assigned, I snapshot the household size via a new `countHousehold(householdId)` helper. It counts existing owners with the matching `householdId` and adds one for the owner being created (which isn't persisted yet). A non-shared owner (`householdId == null`) is a household of one.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 `membershipTier` now returns `\"GOLD\"` when `householdSize >= 3`, taking precedence over the existing `SILVER`/`BRONZE` logic, which is unchanged.\n\nIn the acceptance test, three owners share the same last name + address with `sharesHousehold=true`; the third one's snapshot household size is 3, so its `membershipTier` reads back as `GOLD`. `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
